//oc:doc "The per-role INSIGHT doc (T-3809): the judgement calls and trade-offs this role\nkeeps reaching for. Third block of the role journal, alongside Duty (the role\ndefinition) and Learning (the lessons doc) — the owner asked for it because\ninsight and learning had been sharing one document.\n\n``role_key`` scopes the doc to a role; there is NO ``task_type`` axis (that is\nthe lessons key, and it is deliberately absent here). Since T-e1e3 a role MAY\nhave a factory seed, and unlike lessons that seed is PER-ROLE\n(``seeds/insight_<role_key>.md``) rather than one shared file — the assistant's\njudgement calls would be wrong for any other role. A role with no seed file\nstill reads genuinely EMPTY until it writes.\n\nInsight is SEPARATE, not private. READ is unrestricted: any authenticated\nidentity may read ANY role's insight — the same floor Duty and Learning sit on."
//oc:schema ap=false
type InsightDTO struct {
	//oc:doc "The document size cap now in force, in CHARACTERS (the doc.cap_chars.insight setting). Served on the READ face so an agent can size an edit BEFORE writing it — the alternative is discovering the limit by being refused, and the settings surface is admin-only."
	//oc:field default=0
	CapChars *int `json:"cap_chars"`

	//oc:doc "Size of `text` in CHARACTERS (Unicode code points) — the same unit as cap_chars."
	//oc:field default=0
	SizeChars *int `json:"size_chars"`

	//oc:doc "True when a FACTORY VERSION of this role's insight exists to fall back to — i.e. `seeds/insight_<role_key>.md` ships. It answers ONLY that: it says nothing about whether the doc you are holding IS that factory version (`is_default` answers that), and the two are independent — a role with a seed that has since written its own reads has_seed=true, is_default=false. Added by T-6501 as the precondition for `reset_insight`: a role with has_seed=false gets a 404 from that route, so a surface offering the reset must gate on THIS field. Deliberately NOT named after `RoleDefDTO.is_seed`, which is a fact about the role's DUTY and was misread twice on 2026-08-04 as \"you are reading the factory version\"."
	//oc:field default=false
	HasSeed *bool `json:"has_seed"`

	//oc:doc "True while this role has never written its own insight doc (or reset it). It does NOT imply an empty `text`: a role that ships with a factory seed (`seeds/insight_<role_key>.md`) reads that seed with is_default=true, while a role without one reads \"\". Read this field — not the emptiness of `text` — to tell factory wording apart from something a person wrote. It is NOT the same question as `has_seed`: this one is about what has been WRITTEN, that one about what exists to fall back TO."
	//oc:field default=true
	IsDefault *bool `json:"is_default"`

	//oc:field default=""
	OwnerId *string `json:"owner_id"`

	//oc:field default=""
	RoleKey *string `json:"role_key"`

	//oc:field default=3
	SchemaVersion *int `json:"schema_version"`

	//oc:field default=""
	Text *string `json:"text"`
}

//oc:doc "One ``patch_insight`` edit: replace the occurrence of ``old`` with ``new``. ``old`` must match the current doc EXACTLY ONCE (0 or >1 hits reject the whole batch — the unique anchor doubles as an optimistic concurrency check); an EMPTY ``old`` appends ``new`` at the end of the doc (joined with a newline when the doc does not already end in one)."
