//oc:doc "Hire a roster member (§3.4 #9; pure seam, no UI). The owner assigns the\ndisplay ``name``; the server mints the ``id`` (``m-<hex>`` — never client\nsupplied, it is the attribution key). The member starts offline/active; hiring\ndoes NOT spawn a runtime. ``runtime`` is claude/codex (absent = stored UNSET and resolved at first placement from the host's reported capabilities), and\n``model`` is provider-specific. A blank ``name`` or invalid runtime is a 422.\n\nPRIVILEGE GUARD (closes the hire escalation hole): ``kind`` / ``role_key``\nare PRIVILEGE-BEARING fields — ``kind=\"warden\"`` makes the row a MACHINE\nprincipal (a warden-command target) and ``role_key=\"assistant\"`` makes it an\nADMIN principal (governance capability). A plain hire (name/runtime/model/effort)\nstays open to any authenticated caller (unchanged), but a body carrying a\nnon-empty ``kind`` or ``role_key`` demands the caller itself resolve to at\nleast ``admin_agent`` (the same class the onboard / role-write seams\nrequire) — otherwise 403. Before this guard ANY agent token could self-serve\na warden or an admin member."
//oc:route POST /api/members
//oc:id handle_hire_member_api_members_post
//oc:summary "Hire a member (server mints the id). An omitted runtime is stored UNSET and resolved from the target host's reported runtime capabilities at first placement (a codex-only host grows a codex member) rather than written as claude; only claude/codex are accepted when you do name one; effort defaults to medium and is validated; a hire that names kind or role_key is admin-gated. Answers with a bounded receipt (``id``), not the roster row — call ``get_member`` when you need the rest."
//oc:body application/json req ref=MemberHireDTO
//oc:resp 200 application/json ref=AgentLifecycleReceiptDTO "Successful Response"
//oc:errors std
//oc:mcp {"include":true,"order":6,"name":"hire_member","description":"Hire a member (server mints the id). An omitted runtime is stored UNSET and resolved from the target host's reported runtime capabilities at first placement (a codex-only host grows a codex member) rather than written as claude; only claude/codex are accepted when you do name one; effort defaults to medium and is validated; a hire that names kind or role_key is admin-gated. Answers with a bounded receipt (``id``), not the roster row — call ``get_member`` when you need the rest.","legacy":{"descriptor":"{\n      \"description\": \"Hire a member (server mints the id). An omitted runtime is stored UNSET and resolved from the target host's reported runtime capabilities at first placement (a codex-only host grows a codex member) rather than written as claude; only claude/codex are accepted when you do name one; effort defaults to medium and is validated; a hire that names kind or role_key is admin-gated. Answers with a bounded receipt (``id``), not the roster row \\u2014 call ``get_member`` when you need the rest.\",\n      \"inputSchema\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"effort\": {\n            \"anyOf\": [\n              {\n                \"type\": \"string\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"type\": \"null\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"default\": null,\n            \"title\": \"Effort\"\n          },\n          \"kind\": {\n            \"anyOf\": [\n              {\n                \"type\": \"string\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"type\": \"null\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"default\": null,\n            \"title\": \"Kind\"\n          },\n          \"model\": {\n            \"anyOf\": [\n              {\n                \"type\": \"string\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"type\": \"null\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"default\": null,\n            \"description\": \"Model the new member launches with. There is no model whitelist anywhere in the server: runtime and effort are validated against closed sets and 422 on an unknown value, while this string is stored exactly as sent. A misspelt or retired model name is accepted with 200 and becomes visible only much later, when the member fails to spawn. Blank is legal and leaves the launcher's default.\",\n            \"title\": \"Model\"\n          },\n          \"name\": {\n            \"title\": \"Name\",\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"role_key\": {\n            \"anyOf\": [\n              {\n                \"type\": \"string\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"type\": \"null\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"default\": null,\n            \"description\": \"Role to hire the member into. Supplying it at all is privilege-bearing - a caller below admin-agent is a flat 403 - but the value itself is never checked against the role table: a key nobody defined is stored verbatim and the member is created, 200. Your role_key is echoed back unchanged, so the only thing in the response that separates a typo from a real role is role_name, which comes back as an empty string.\",\n            \"title\": \"Role Key\"\n          },\n          \"runtime\": {\n            \"anyOf\": [\n              {\n                \"enum\": [\n                  \"claude\",\n                  \"codex\"\n                ],\n                \"type\": \"string\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"type\": \"null\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"default\": null,\n            \"title\": \"Runtime\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"name\"\n        ],\n        \"additionalProperties\": false,\n        \"type\": \"object\"\n      },\n      \"name\": \"hire_member\"\n    }"}}
func HandleHireMemberApiMembersPost(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
}

