//oc:doc "The reply-card list — LIGHT rows (``list_reply_cards`` MCP tool; owner ruling:\n卡只需要 title+決策). ``?status=waiting`` (the default) returns cards still\nwaiting on the owner, longest-waiting first; ``?status=answered`` returns cards\nanswered within the last 24h, newest answer first; ``?status=expired`` returns\ncards the owner marked expired within the last 24h (keyed off ``expired_ts``),\nnewest first. Each row carries the card's\n``summary`` (its title) and — on an answered row — the decision DIGEST\n(every circled option's index + original wording, an answer-text preview, the\nattachment count), NEVER the ``body`` or the full ``options`` text; pull one\ncard in full with ``get_reply_card``. ``?limit=N`` (N > 0) caps the rows AFTER\nthe pane's ordering (the pane's first N survive); absent / non-positive = the\nwhole pane.\n\nTHERE IS ONE SHAPE AND IT IS THE LIGHT ROW. The ``?view=full`` projection is\nGONE (owner ruling 2026-09-07): a second response shape on one route made every\nreader special-case which arm it was holding, and the round trips it saved were\nspent drawing whole cards nobody had opened. The cockpit's panes now render the\nlight row COLLAPSED and fetch ``get_reply_card`` for the ONE card the owner\nopens — the same posture the inline chat card has always had — so a whole pane\ncosts one request and an unopened card costs none. ``view`` is not accepted;\nlike any other unknown query parameter it is ignored."
//oc:route GET /api/reply-cards
//oc:id handle_list_reply_cards_api_reply_cards_get
//oc:summary "List light reply-card rows (summary and decision digest, without the full body/options). status is waiting (the default, longest-waiting first), answered (the last 24 hours) or expired (the last 24 hours); a positive limit is applied after each pane is ordered. Read one card in full with get_reply_card."
//oc:param query status union=[{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]
//oc:param query limit union=[{"type":"integer"},{"type":"null"}]
//oc:resp 200 application/json inline={"items":{"$ref":"#/components/schemas/ReplyCardListItemDTO"},"type":"array","title":"Response Handle List Reply Cards Api Reply Cards Get"} "Successful Response"
//oc:errors std
//oc:mcp {"include":true,"order":32,"name":"list_reply_cards","description":"List light reply-card rows (summary and decision digest, without the full body/options). status is waiting (the default, longest-waiting first), answered (the last 24 hours) or expired (the last 24 hours); a positive limit is applied after each pane is ordered. Read one card in full with get_reply_card.","legacy":{"descriptor":"{\n      \"description\": \"List light reply-card rows (summary and decision digest, without the full body/options). status is waiting (the default, longest-waiting first), answered (the last 24 hours) or expired (the last 24 hours); a positive limit is applied after each pane is ordered. Read one card in full with get_reply_card.\",\n      \"inputSchema\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"limit\": {\n            \"anyOf\": [\n              {\n                \"type\": \"integer\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"type\": \"null\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"default\": null,\n            \"description\": \"Maximum number of cards to return. It only ever truncates: 0, a negative value, or omitting the field all mean the WHOLE pane - never an empty result, never an error - and a value larger than the pane is silently harmless. So 'limit: 0' does not mean 'none'; if you pass 0 as a computed default you fetch everything. And since the answer is a plain list with no total and no truncation flag, a full pane and a truncated one look exactly the same.\",\n            \"title\": \"Limit\"\n          },\n          \"status\": {\n            \"anyOf\": [\n              {\n                \"type\": \"string\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"type\": \"null\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"default\": null,\n            \"title\": \"Status\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"type\": \"object\"\n      },\n      \"name\": \"list_reply_cards\"\n    }"}}
func HandleListReplyCardsApiReplyCardsGet(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request, status any, limit any) {
}

//oc:doc "Open a reply card (agent-side; the MCP tool ``create_reply_card``). The initiator is ALWAYS the verified JWT ``sub``. Server validation: ``kind`` must be ``decision``|``action``; ``summary`` must be non-blank; ``options`` must be 1..4 objects ``{\"text\", \"ai_pick\"}`` with non-blank ``text``, and ``ai_pick`` — not position — is what marks the AI recommendation; ``select_mode`` is ``single`` (default) or ``multi``, and a ``single`` card may carry at most one ``ai_pick`` option — violations are a 400. Opening a card ALSO posts one chat message (initiator → owner, body = summary, ``meta.reply_card_id`` = the card id) so the ask rides the normal chat stream (unread red dot, permanent history); the card's ``chat_message_id`` links back to it. TASK/STEP BINDING IS DECLARED, NEVER INFERRED (T-18): ``linked_task`` is a REQUIRED field. ``null`` opens a plain unbound 請示. ``{task_id, step_id}`` binds the card to that step — the step enters ``waiting_owner`` carrying the card (``reply_card_id``), and the task follows into ``waiting_owner`` unless the step sits in a parallel group (sibling lanes may still run). The caller must be the task's executor (403 otherwise); the task must be ``in_progress``|``waiting_owner`` (409); the step must belong to the task (404) and must not be terminal — ``done``/``superseded`` (409). A ``linked_task`` object carrying a ``task_id`` but no ``step_id`` is a 400: a card bound to a task but to no step places no ``waiting_owner`` hold, so the task would run on to ``done`` underneath an ask the owner can then never answer (T-4166). OMITTING ``linked_task`` is a 400 naming both legal shapes — the field exists so that not deciding is impossible to do silently, which is exactly what the old auto-binding did whenever it could not resolve a step. Fans one ``chat`` and one ``reply_card`` SSE delta (plus a ``task`` delta when a step was bound)."
//oc:route POST /api/reply-cards
//oc:id handle_create_reply_card_api_reply_cards_post
//oc:summary "Open a reply card: an ask the owner must answer (options ≤4 on a single card, ≤20 on a multi card, each carrying its own ai_pick flag; select_mode single|multi). linked_task is REQUIRED and has no default — every card must SAY whether it is about a task, because the server no longer infers one. Send linked_task={\"task_id\": ..., \"step_id\": ...} to bind the ask to the step it is about: that step (and its task) enters waiting_owner until the owner answers. Send linked_task=null when the ask is not about a task — it opens as a plain unbound 請示. BOTH ids are required in the object form: a task_id with NO step_id is a 400, because a card bound to a task but to no step places no 等我回覆 hold, so the task would finish underneath your question and the owner's answer would then be rejected for good. Omitting linked_task entirely is a 400 that names both legal shapes. Optional attachments ride the question (same shape as post_chat: {id} from `ocagent upload` / POST /api/chat/attachments, or inline data_b64). Answers with a bounded receipt (``id``, ``chat_message_id``, ``created_ts``, ``attachments``), not the card — call ``get_reply_card`` when you need the rest."
//oc:body application/json req ref=ReplyCardCreateDTO
//oc:resp 200 application/json ref=ReplyCardCreateReceiptDTO "Successful Response"
//oc:errors std
//oc:mcp {"include":true,"order":31,"name":"create_reply_card","description":"Open a reply card: an ask the owner must answer (options ≤4 on a single card, ≤20 on a multi card, each carrying its own ai_pick flag; select_mode single|multi). linked_task is REQUIRED and has no default — every card must SAY whether it is about a task, because the server no longer infers one. Send linked_task={\"task_id\": ..., \"step_id\": ...} to bind the ask to the step it is about: that step (and its task) enters waiting_owner until the owner answers. Send linked_task=null when the ask is not about a task — it opens as a plain unbound 請示. BOTH ids are required in the object form: a task_id with NO step_id is a 400, because a card bound to a task but to no step places no 等我回覆 hold, so the task would finish underneath your question and the owner's answer would then be rejected for good. Omitting linked_task entirely is a 400 that names both legal shapes. Optional attachments ride the question (same shape as post_chat: {id} from `ocagent upload` / POST /api/chat/attachments, or inline data_b64). Answers with a bounded receipt (``id``, ``chat_message_id``, ``created_ts``, ``attachments``), not the card — call ``get_reply_card`` when you need the rest.","legacy":{"descriptor":"{\n      \"description\": \"Open a reply card: an ask the owner must answer (options \\u22644 on a single card, \\u226420 on a multi card, each carrying its own ai_pick flag; select_mode single|multi). linked_task is REQUIRED and has no default \\u2014 every card must SAY whether it is about a task, because the server no longer infers one. Send linked_task={\\\"task_id\\\": ..., \\\"step_id\\\": ...} to bind the ask to the step it is about: that step (and its task) enters waiting_owner until the owner answers. Send linked_task=null when the ask is not about a task \\u2014 it opens as a plain unbound \\u8acb\\u793a. BOTH ids are required in the object form: a task_id with NO step_id is a 400, because a card bound to a task but to no step places no \\u7b49\\u6211\\u56de\\u8986 hold, so the task would finish underneath your question and the owner's answer would then be rejected for good. Omitting linked_task entirely is a 400 that names both legal shapes. Optional attachments ride the question (same shape as post_chat: {id} from `ocagent upload` / POST /api/chat/attachments, or inline data_b64). Answers with a bounded receipt (``id``, ``chat_message_id``, ``created_ts``, ``attachments``), not the card \\u2014 call ``get_reply_card`` when you need the rest.\",\n      \"inputSchema\": {\n        \"$defs\": {\n          \"ReplyCardOptionDTO\": {\n            \"description\": \"One quick-reply choice. text is the wording; ai_pick marks THIS option as your own recommendation and is the ONLY carrier of that fact - the old convention that options[0] was the AI pick is gone, and position now means nothing. On a single card at most one option may set ai_pick (two is a 400); on a multi card any number may, zero included.\",\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"ai_pick\": {\n                \"default\": false,\n                \"title\": \"Ai Pick\",\n                \"type\": \"boolean\"\n              },\n              \"text\": {\n                \"title\": \"Text\",\n                \"type\": \"string\"\n              }\n            },\n            \"required\": [\n              \"text\"\n            ],\n            \"title\": \"ReplyCardOptionDTO\",\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"additionalProperties\": false\n          },\n          \"ReplyCardLinkDTO\": {\n            \"description\": \"The task/step this ask is about. BOTH ids are required: a card bound to a task but to no step places no \\u7b49\\u6211\\u56de\\u8986 hold, so the task keeps running past the question and the owner's answer is later refused.\",\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"step_id\": {\n                \"title\": \"Step Id\",\n                \"type\": \"string\"\n              },\n              \"task_id\": {\n                \"title\": \"Task Id\",\n                \"type\": \"string\"\n              }\n            },\n            \"required\": [\n              \"task_id\",\n              \"step_id\"\n            ],\n            \"title\": \"ReplyCardLinkDTO\",\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"additionalProperties\": false\n          },\n          \"ChatAttachmentInputDTO\": {\n            \"description\": \"An attachment carried on a posted chat message \\u2014 either INLINE BYTES or a\\nREFERENCE to a blob already in the shared attachment store.\\n\\nInline: ``data_b64`` is the bytes, base64-encoded \\u2014 a data-URI\\n(``data:<mime>;base64,....``) OR bare base64 (the handler strips a\\n``data:...;base64,`` prefix if present). ``mime`` and ``filename`` are\\noptional: an omitted ``mime`` is sniffed for images (else\\n``application/octet-stream``); an omitted ``filename`` defaults for pasted\\nimages.\\n\\nReference: ``id`` names an EXISTING blob (minted by\\n``POST /api/chat/attachments`` \\u2014 the streaming upload seam that keeps file\\nbytes out of a JSON tool call). The stored blob's mime/filename are\\nauthoritative: ``filename``/``mime`` sent alongside ``id`` are IGNORED (so\\nthe upload response ``{id, mime, filename}`` can be pasted back verbatim).\\nAn unknown ``id`` is a 400; carrying BOTH ``id`` and ``data_b64`` is a 400\\n(ambiguous intent). An item with neither ``id`` nor ``data_b64`` is a\\n400 (T-e2b2: it used to be dropped silently, so a sender that named a file it\\nnever sent got a success and the recipient got nothing). The reply-card ANSWER face is\\ninline-only: it decodes ``data_b64`` and has never resolved ``id`` references,\\nso an item carrying only an ``id`` there is a 400 (T-e2b2 — it used to be\\ndropped silently).\\n\\n``filename`` is capped at 128 CHARACTERS (Unicode runes, so 128 CJK characters fit \\u2014 it is not a byte count) on BOTH paths, inline and the streaming upload seam; a longer one is REFUSED with a 400 and never truncated. The cap binds NEW writes only.\",\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"data_b64\": {\n                \"default\": \"\",\n                \"title\": \"Data B64\",\n                \"type\": \"string\"\n              },\n              \"filename\": {\n                \"anyOf\": [\n                  {\n                    \"type\": \"string\"\n                  },\n                  {\n                    \"type\": \"null\"\n                  }\n                ],\n                \"default\": null,\n                \"title\": \"Filename\"\n              },\n              \"id\": {\n                \"anyOf\": [\n                  {\n                    \"type\": \"string\"\n                  },\n                  {\n                    \"type\": \"null\"\n                  }\n                ],\n                \"default\": null,\n                \"title\": \"Id\"\n              },\n              \"mime\": {\n                \"anyOf\": [\n                  {\n                    \"type\": \"string\"\n                  },\n                  {\n                    \"type\": \"null\"\n                  }\n                ],\n                \"default\": null,\n                \"title\": \"Mime\"\n              }\n            },\n            \"title\": \"ChatAttachmentInputDTO\",\n            \"type\": \"object\",\n            \"additionalProperties\": false\n          }\n        },\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"attachments\": {\n            \"items\": {\n              \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ChatAttachmentInputDTO\"\n            },\n            \"title\": \"Attachments\",\n            \"type\": \"array\"\n          },\n          \"body\": {\n            \"default\": \"\",\n            \"description\": \"The question's full text - the part that lets the owner decide without going and looking things up. It is stored as sent with NO validation, so OMITTING it is not an error: the card is created with an empty body and answers 200, and what reaches the owner is a summary line and some options with no reasoning attached. Nothing warns you; the card simply arrives thinner than you meant it to.\",\n            \"title\": \"Body\",\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"kind\": {\n            \"enum\": [\n              \"decision\",\n              \"action\"\n            ],\n            \"title\": \"Kind\",\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"linked_task\": {\n            \"anyOf\": [\n              {\n                \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ReplyCardLinkDTO\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"type\": \"null\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"description\": \"REQUIRED \\u2014 declare it, the server never infers it. ``null`` = this ask is NOT about a task (a plain unbound \\u8acb\\u793a). ``{\\\"task_id\\\": ..., \\\"step_id\\\": ...}`` binds the ask to that step, which enters waiting_owner until the owner answers. BOTH ids are required: a task_id with no step_id is a 400, because binding a task without a step places no \\u7b49\\u6211\\u56de\\u8986 hold and the task would run past your question. Omitting the field is a 400 that names both legal shapes.\",\n            \"title\": \"Linked Task\"\n          },\n          \"options\": {\n            \"items\": {\n              \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ReplyCardOptionDTO\"\n            },\n            \"title\": \"Options\",\n            \"type\": \"array\"\n          },\n          \"select_mode\": {\n            \"default\": \"single\",\n            \"description\": \"How many options the owner may circle: single (the default - at most one, and at most one option may carry ai_pick) or multi (any number). It is a SEPARATE axis from kind: kind says what the owner must DO (decide / act), select_mode says how many choices the answer may carry. A single card refuses an answer carrying two indices, and refuses a create marking two options ai_pick.\",\n            \"enum\": [\n              \"single\",\n              \"multi\"\n            ],\n            \"title\": \"Select Mode\",\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"summary\": {\n            \"title\": \"Summary\",\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"kind\",\n          \"summary\",\n          \"options\",\n          \"linked_task\"\n        ],\n        \"additionalProperties\": false,\n        \"type\": \"object\"\n      },\n      \"name\": \"create_reply_card\"\n    }"}}
func HandleCreateReplyCardApiReplyCardsPost(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
}

