//oc:doc "Answer a WAITING reply card — the only POSITIVE close (there is deliberately no close/skip surface; the expire action is the sole other exit and is NOT an answer — open to the card's own author as well as the owner / an admin agent (T-6020 held it at the admin floor; T-1b88, owner 2026-08-07, widened it to the author)). The answer is an ``option_idxs`` LIST and/or free ``text`` (+ attachments); an empty answer is 400 — and ``option_idxs: []`` IS empty, not an answer — an out-of-range index is 400, and a ``single`` card given two indices is 400. The stored list is deduped and sorted ascending, so ``[2,0]`` and ``[0,2]`` are the same stored answer. Any real answer — including a counter-question typed as text — flips the card to ``answered`` and stamps ``answered_ts``; if the reply did not settle the original question the agent opens a NEW card (never reopens this one). Answering an already-answered card is a 409 (revise via PUT instead); an expired card is a 409 too (terminal — if the question still matters the agent opens a NEW card). When the card is bound to a task step (create_reply_card with an explicit ``linked_task``), the FIRST answer also releases the waiting_owner hold — the server restores the step (and the task, once its last bound card is answered) to in_progress; the agent then advances the work itself. Fans one ``reply_card`` SSE delta (badge −1; the agent's own connection receives it and refetches the card for the full answer context)."
//oc:route POST /api/reply-cards/{card_id}/answer
//oc:id handle_answer_reply_card_api_reply_cards__card_id__answer_post
//oc:summary "Answer a waiting reply card — the only way a card closes."
//oc:param path card_id req
//oc:body application/json req ref=ReplyCardAnswerPostDTO
//oc:resp 200 application/json ref=ReplyCardReceiptDTO "Successful Response"
//oc:errors std
//oc:mcp {"include":true,"order":35,"name":"answer_reply_card","description":"Answer a waiting reply card — the only positive close. Answers with a bounded receipt (``id``, ``status``, ``answered_ts``, ``expired_ts``, ``answer``, ``task_id``, ``step_id``), not the whole card — call ``get_reply_card`` when you need the rest.","legacy":{"descriptor":"{\n      \"description\": \"Answer a waiting reply card \\u2014 the only positive close. Answers with a bounded receipt (``id``, ``status``, ``answered_ts``, ``expired_ts``, ``answer``, ``task_id``, ``step_id``), not the whole card \\u2014 call ``get_reply_card`` when you need the rest.\",\n      \"inputSchema\": {\n        \"$defs\": {\n          \"ChatAttachmentInputDTO\": {\n            \"description\": \"An attachment carried on a posted chat message \\u2014 either INLINE BYTES or a\\nREFERENCE to a blob already in the shared attachment store.\\n\\nInline: ``data_b64`` is the bytes, base64-encoded \\u2014 a data-URI\\n(``data:<mime>;base64,....``) OR bare base64 (the handler strips a\\n``data:...;base64,`` prefix if present). ``mime`` and ``filename`` are\\noptional: an omitted ``mime`` is sniffed for images (else\\n``application/octet-stream``); an omitted ``filename`` defaults for pasted\\nimages.\\n\\nReference: ``id`` names an EXISTING blob (minted by\\n``POST /api/chat/attachments`` \\u2014 the streaming upload seam that keeps file\\nbytes out of a JSON tool call). The stored blob's mime/filename are\\nauthoritative: ``filename``/``mime`` sent alongside ``id`` are IGNORED (so\\nthe upload response ``{id, mime, filename}`` can be pasted back verbatim).\\nAn unknown ``id`` is a 400; carrying BOTH ``id`` and ``data_b64`` is a 400\\n(ambiguous intent). An item with neither ``id`` nor ``data_b64`` is a\\n400 (T-e2b2: it used to be dropped silently, so a sender that named a file it\\nnever sent got a success and the recipient got nothing). The reply-card ANSWER face is\\ninline-only: it decodes ``data_b64`` and has never resolved ``id`` references,\\nso an item carrying only an ``id`` there is a 400 (T-e2b2 — it used to be\\ndropped silently).\\n\\n``filename`` is capped at 128 CHARACTERS (Unicode runes, so 128 CJK characters fit \\u2014 it is not a byte count) on BOTH paths, inline and the streaming upload seam; a longer one is REFUSED with a 400 and never truncated. The cap binds NEW writes only.\",\n            \"properties\": {\n              \"data_b64\": {\n                \"default\": \"\",\n                \"title\": \"Data B64\",\n                \"type\": \"string\"\n              },\n              \"filename\": {\n                \"anyOf\": [\n                  {\n                    \"type\": \"string\"\n                  },\n                  {\n                    \"type\": \"null\"\n                  }\n                ],\n                \"title\": \"Filename\"\n              },\n              \"id\": {\n                \"anyOf\": [\n                  {\n                    \"type\": \"string\"\n                  },\n                  {\n                    \"type\": \"null\"\n                  }\n                ],\n                \"title\": \"Id\"\n              },\n              \"mime\": {\n                \"anyOf\": [\n                  {\n                    \"type\": \"string\"\n                  },\n                  {\n                    \"type\": \"null\"\n                  }\n                ],\n                \"title\": \"Mime\"\n              }\n            },\n            \"title\": \"ChatAttachmentInputDTO\",\n            \"additionalProperties\": false,\n            \"type\": \"object\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"attachments\": {\n            \"items\": {\n              \"$ref\": \"#/$defs/ChatAttachmentInputDTO\"\n            },\n            \"title\": \"Attachments\",\n            \"type\": \"array\"\n          },\n          \"card_id\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          \"option_idxs\": {\n            \"anyOf\": [\n              {\n                \"items\": {\n                  \"type\": \"integer\"\n                },\n                \"type\": \"array\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"type\": \"null\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"default\": null,\n            \"description\": \"Indices into the card's options of every option you circle. Omit it or send null to answer with text/attachments only; an EMPTY list is not an answer and is a 400, exactly like sending nothing. Order and duplicates do not matter - the server stores the list deduped and ascending, so [2,0] and [0,2] end up byte-identical. Every index must be in range; a single-select card accepts at most one.\",\n            \"title\": \"Option Idxs\"\n          },\n          \"text\": {\n            \"default\": \"\",\n            \"description\": \"Free-text answer. An answer must carry at least one of option_idxs, text or an attachment (400 otherwise), but text and option_idxs are stored INDEPENDENTLY and nothing cross-checks them. So pasting an option's wording in here instead of sending its index succeeds with 200 and records option_idxs as null - byte for byte what a deliberate free-text answer looks like. The reader cannot tell that a listed option was chosen. If you mean to pick options, send their indices.\",\n            \"title\": \"Text\",\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"card_id\"\n        ],\n        \"additionalProperties\": false,\n        \"type\": \"object\"\n      },\n      \"name\": \"answer_reply_card\"\n    }"}}
func HandleAnswerReplyCardApiReplyCardsCardIdAnswerPost(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request, cardId string) {
}

//oc:doc "Revise an ANSWERED card's answer (重新決定 — the owner changing their OWN answer; distinct from the agent asking again via a new card). Same body + validation as POST; the card MUST already be answered (a waiting card is a 409 — answer it with POST). The answer is replaced wholesale, ``answered_ts`` re-stamps (the card re-enters the 24h recently-answered window), and status STAYS ``answered`` — a revision never reopens the card or re-counts the badge. Fans one ``reply_card`` SSE delta so the agent picks up the updated decision."
//oc:route PUT /api/reply-cards/{card_id}/answer
//oc:id handle_reanswer_reply_card_api_reply_cards__card_id__answer_put
//oc:summary "Revise an answered card's answer (重新決定): stays answered. Answers with a bounded receipt (``id``, ``status``, ``answered_ts``, ``expired_ts``, ``answer``, ``task_id``, ``step_id``), not the whole card — call ``get_reply_card`` when you need the rest."
//oc:param path card_id req
//oc:body application/json req ref=ReplyCardAnswerPostDTO
//oc:resp 200 application/json ref=ReplyCardReceiptDTO "Successful Response"
//oc:errors std
