//oc:doc "``report_waking()`` — the boot report (identity from token, NO member_id).\n\nStamps the CALLER's ``waking_since`` → derives *waking* until the SSE connects\n(⇒ online) or the wall-clock TTL lapses. ``online`` is untouched (pure SSE\nprojection).\n\nRECYCLE LOOP BREAK: a fresh session's FIRST report clears ALL the recycle markers\n— ``refocus_since`` / ``stopped_since`` / ``stopping_since`` → 0.0 — so the\nrespawned agent sheds the refocus intent, the dump-done stamp AND the graceful-\nshutdown anchor BEFORE it goes online. The boot序 guarantees this report lands\nbefore the SSE connects, so the new session can never inherit a stale marker and\nre-trigger a recycle (or derive *stopping*) on itself.\n\n``model`` is optional runtime telemetry. The server stores it as ``actual_model``\nwithout changing the owner-configured launch model."
//oc:route POST /api/self/waking
//oc:id handle_report_waking_api_self_waking_post
//oc:summary "report_waking(): stamp the caller's waking + clear recycle markers. Answers with a bounded receipt (``id``, ``desired_state``, ``refocus_op``, ``refocus_deadline``), not the member row — call ``get_member`` when you need the rest."
//oc:body application/json req ref=ReportWakingDTO
//oc:resp 200 application/json ref=SelfReportReceiptDTO "Successful Response"
//oc:errors std
//oc:mcp {"include":true,"order":13,"name":"report_waking","description":"report_waking(): stamp the caller's waking + clear recycle markers. Answers with a bounded receipt (``id``, ``desired_state``, ``refocus_op``, ``refocus_deadline``), not the member row — call ``get_member`` when you need the rest.","legacy":{"descriptor":"{\n      \"description\": \"report_waking(): stamp the caller's waking + clear recycle markers. Answers with a bounded receipt (``id``, ``desired_state``, ``refocus_op``, ``refocus_deadline``), not the member row — call ``get_member`` when you need the rest.\",\n      \"inputSchema\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"model\": {\n            \"anyOf\": [\n              {\n                \"type\": \"string\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"type\": \"null\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"default\": null,\n            \"description\": \"The model this session actually came up on. It is written verbatim into the member's actual_model - the value the roster and the monitoring view show as what this member is really running - with no validation and no comparison against the model that was requested. Omitting it is not an error and clears nothing: the field keeps whatever the previous session reported, so a session that wakes on a different model and stays quiet leaves the cockpit displaying a model nobody is running. Report what you are on, not what you were asked for.\",\n            \"title\": \"Model\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"additionalProperties\": false,\n        \"type\": \"object\"\n      },\n      \"name\": \"report_waking\"\n    }"}}
func HandleReportWakingApiSelfWakingPost(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
}

//oc:doc "Read the org-adjustable settings (owner or admin agent — T-6020). The response IS the field list — SettingsDTO — so this line deliberately names none of them: it used to name three, plus a read-only `self-healed port` that is not on this DTO at all any more, while the surface grew past twenty and nothing ever went red. Read a value here before writing it back through update_settings."
