//oc:doc "Partially update the org-adjustable settings (owner or admin agent — T-6020). Only supplied\nfields change; a change is durable (DB) AND live immediately — `owner_token_ttl`\napplies from the next login, `agent_token_ttl` from the next bootstrap, reconcile,\nor outsource spawn, and the offboard points from the next context report. Either\nTTL outside the 12h/24h/7d/30d whitelist, `handover_pct` outside 40..90, or a\nnotice point that does not sit strictly below its final one (`notice_pct` vs\n`handover_pct`, `codex_notice_round` vs `codex_compaction_threshold`) is a 422\n(nothing is written)."
//oc:route PATCH /api/settings
//oc:id handle_update_settings_api_settings_patch
//oc:summary "Edit the org-adjustable settings (owner/admin agent) — only the fields you send change, and the change is live immediately. This tool's input schema is the field list; read the current values with get_settings first."
//oc:body application/json req ref=SettingsUpdateDTO
//oc:resp 200 application/json ref=SettingsDTO "Successful Response"
//oc:errors std
//oc:mcp {"include":true,"order":2,"name":"update_settings","description":"Edit the org-adjustable settings (owner/admin agent) — only the fields you send change, and the change is live immediately. This tool's input schema is the field list; read the current values with get_settings first.","legacy":{"descriptor":"{\n  \"description\": \"Edit the org-adjustable settings (owner/admin agent) — only the fields you send change, and the change is live immediately. This tool's input schema is the field list; read the current values with get_settings first.\",\n  \"inputSchema\": {\n    \"properties\": {\n      \"codex_compaction_threshold\": {\n        \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"integer\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"description\": \"Codex context-compaction threshold, 1 through 10.\",\n        \"title\": \"Codex Compaction Threshold\"\n      },\n      \"backup_retain\": {\n        \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"integer\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"description\": \"How many database backup files rotation KEEPS — N; everything past N is DELETED from disk (it used to be moved to a trash/ nobody emptied). Must be between 1 and 20. Two things it does NOT mean: N counts VERSIONS, not DAYS — the calendar depth depends on how many backups those days produced; and N is PER POOL, not per directory — routine (scheduled + manual) and pre-migration backups hold separate quotas, so 5 keeps up to 10 files. Read the current value from get_settings rather than assuming a number.\",\n        \"title\": \"Backup Retain\"\n      },\n      \"chat_budget_chars\": {\n        \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"integer\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"description\": \"The wake snapshot's chat block budget, in CHARACTERS (Unicode code points). It is what bounds resume_summary's chat block AND the estimated_total_chars peek_resume_summary_size reports — one number, one code path, so the two can never disagree. Must be between 1000 and 13000. Unlike the doc_cap_chars_* knobs it may be LOWERED as well as raised (the block is repacked on every read, not stored). Read the current value from get_settings rather than assuming a number.\",\n        \"title\": \"Chat Budget Chars\"\n      },\n      \"step_note_cap_chars\": {\n        \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"integer\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"description\": \"The size cap on one task step's working note, in CHARACTERS (Unicode code points). Must be between 1000 and 100000. Unlike the doc_cap_chars_* knobs it may be LOWERED as well as raised, because it is enforced only when a note is WRITTEN: a note already stored above a lowered cap stays readable in full and only becomes uneditable. It does NOT govern the task-level handover note or a chat message body, which keep their own 4,000-character constant. Read the current value from get_settings rather than assuming a number.\",\n        \"title\": \"Step Note Cap Chars\"\n      },\n      \"doc_cap_chars_boot_sequence\": {\n        \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"integer\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"description\": \"The size cap on a 啟動步驟 block of the boot context, in CHARACTERS (Unicode code points). ONE knob for BOTH runtimes (claude and codex), each document measured on its own text. Must be at least this document's shipped default and at most 100000. Read the current values from get_settings rather than assuming a number.\",\n        \"title\": \"Doc Cap Chars Boot Sequence\"\n      },\n      \"doc_cap_chars_duty\": {\n        \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"integer\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"description\": \"The size cap on a role's DUTY doc (the role definition), in CHARACTERS (Unicode code points). Must be at least this segment's own shipped default — which is deliberately much smaller than the other three segments' — and at most 100000. Read the current values from get_settings rather than assuming a number.\",\n        \"title\": \"Doc Cap Chars Duty\"\n      },\n      \"doc_cap_chars_insight\": {\n        \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"integer\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"description\": \"The size cap on a role's INSIGHT doc, in CHARACTERS (Unicode code points). Must be at least this segment's shipped default and at most 100000. Read the current values from get_settings rather than assuming a number.\",\n        \"title\": \"Doc Cap Chars Insight\"\n      },\n      \"doc_cap_chars_learning\": {\n        \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"integer\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"description\": \"The size cap on a role's LEARNING doc (the lessons doc), in CHARACTERS (Unicode code points). Must be at least this segment's shipped default and at most 100000. Read the current values from get_settings rather than assuming a number.\",\n        \"title\": \"Doc Cap Chars Learning\"\n      },\n      \"doc_cap_chars_manual_learnings\": {\n        \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"integer\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"description\": \"The size cap on a TASK MANUAL's learnings doc, in CHARACTERS (Unicode code points). Must be at least this segment's shipped default and at most 100000. Read the current values from get_settings rather than assuming a number.\",\n        \"title\": \"Doc Cap Chars Manual Learnings\"\n      },\n      \"doc_cap_chars_manual_sop\": {\n        \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"integer\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"description\": \"The size cap on a TASK MANUAL's sop_md doc, in CHARACTERS (Unicode code points). Must be at least this segment's shipped default and at most 100000. Read the current values from get_settings rather than assuming a number.\",\n        \"title\": \"Doc Cap Chars Manual Sop\"\n      },\n      \"doc_cap_chars_offboard\": {\n        \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"integer\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"description\": \"The size cap on the 〈停止〉 block, in CHARACTERS (Unicode code points). Must be at least this document's shipped default and at most 100000. Read the current values from get_settings rather than assuming a number.\",\n        \"title\": \"Doc Cap Chars Offboard\"\n      },\n      \"doc_cap_chars_system_interaction\": {\n        \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"integer\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"description\": \"The size cap on the 系統互動 block of the boot context, in CHARACTERS (Unicode code points). Must be at least this document's shipped default and at most 100000. Read the current values from get_settings rather than assuming a number.\",\n        \"title\": \"Doc Cap Chars System Interaction\"\n      },\n      \"display_language\": {\n        \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"description\": \"The owner's cockpit language (T-0b41-p2) — trimmed; \\\"\\\" clears it back to unset. Must be one of zh, en (or \\\"\\\"); anything else is a 422.\",\n        \"title\": \"Display Language\"\n      },\n      \"display_theme\": {\n        \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"description\": \"The owner's cockpit visual theme (T-0b41-p2) — trimmed; \\\"\\\" clears it back to unset. Must be one of office, xian (or \\\"\\\"); anything else is a 422.\",\n        \"title\": \"Display Theme\"\n      },\n      \"display_wide\": {\n        \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"description\": \"Turn the WIDE cockpit layout on/off (T-756f) — true lifts the centred ~1040px content column (the side gutters stay), false restores it. A plain boolean with no unset state: omit the field to leave it unchanged.\",\n        \"title\": \"Display Wide\"\n      },\n      \"handover_pct\": {\n        \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"integer\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"description\": \"The SECOND offboard point: the FINAL notice, and where the automatic handover fires. 40..90, and strictly greater than notice_pct (the pair is validated together against the POST-patch values, so either one may be sent alone).\",\n        \"title\": \"Handover Pct\"\n      },\n      \"notice_pct\": {\n        \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"integer\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"description\": \"The FIRST offboard point (T-a9d6): the SOFT notice, where the agent is asked to work the offboard sequence and then call report_stopped itself. 1..89, and strictly below handover_pct.\",\n        \"title\": \"Notice Pct\"\n      },\n      \"codex_notice_round\": {\n        \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"integer\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"description\": \"The codex SOFT-notice compaction round (T-a9d6). 1..10, and strictly below codex_compaction_threshold.\",\n        \"title\": \"Codex Notice Round\"\n      },\n      \"monitoring_refresh_seconds\": {\n        \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"integer\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"description\": \"Minimum interval between monitoring and machine refreshes, in seconds (1 through 60).\",\n        \"title\": \"Monitoring Refresh Seconds\"\n      },\n      \"accelerated_grace_secs\": {\n        \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"integer\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"description\": \"加速停止 grace, in seconds. Must be 10 through 3600. Applies to every CLOCKED wind-down cause at once (the second context threshold and the owner-pressed 加速停止); it can never put a clock on a soft cause.\",\n        \"title\": \"Accelerated Grace Secs\"\n      },\n      \"warden_credential_lifetime_secs\": {\n        \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"integer\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"description\": \"How long a MACHINE (warden) credential is meant to live, in seconds. Must be 86400 through 34560000 (one day through 400 days). A warden renews its own credential once that credential is two thirds of this old, plus a per-machine stagger of up to one hour so that LOWERING this value does not put the whole fleet on the mint endpoint inside one poll. The floor is one day because the last third of the lifetime is the retry window: at the 15-minute poll a one-day lifetime still leaves about 32 attempts. Wardens pick a change up within one poll interval. Warden credentials carry no `exp` today, so this governs renewal only and nothing expires because of it. Read the current value from get_settings rather than assuming a number.\",\n        \"title\": \"Warden Credential Lifetime Secs\"\n      },\n      \"org_name\": {\n        \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"description\": \"The studio display name (T-d693) — trimmed, max 80 runes; \\\"\\\" clears it back to the localized default. A value longer than 80 runes is a 422.\",\n        \"title\": \"Org Name\"\n      },\n      \"outsource_max_parallel\": {\n        \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"integer\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"title\": \"Outsource Max Parallel\"\n      },\n      \"owner_name\": {\n        \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"description\": \"The owner's display nickname (T-0b41) — trimmed, max 80 runes; \\\"\\\" clears it back to the localized default. A value longer than 80 runes is a 422.\",\n        \"title\": \"Owner Name\"\n      },\n      \"push_contact_email\": {\n        \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"description\": \"The push contact address (T-8a82) — trimmed, max 254 runes; \\\"\\\" clears it back to unset and stops all Web Push delivery. A value must be a single `local@domain` address whose domain is a real public one: a malformed address, or one on a reserved suffix (.local, .localhost, .internal, .test, .invalid, .example), is a 422 — those are exactly the values the push gateways reject with BadJwtToken, which would take push down silently.\",\n        \"title\": \"Push Contact Email\"\n      },\n      \"suggested_replies_reply_card\": {\n        \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n            \"items\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"type\": \"array\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"description\": \"Replace the 建議回覆 list offered under a 請示卡 reply box (T-122) wholesale — one sentence per entry, the owner's own writing. At most 20 entries, each trimmed and at most 120 runes (Unicode code points); over either bound is a 422 that writes NOTHING, and the list is never silently truncated. An EXPLICIT EMPTY ARRAY IS LEGAL and means \\\"offer no suggestions there\\\" — unlike the scheduled-message custom_* sets, where [] is a 422. Blank entries are dropped. Read the current list from get_settings before sending: this replaces it, it does not append. 🔴 null is NOT \\\"clear\\\": an omitted field and an explicit null both mean LEAVE THIS LIST UNCHANGED, so an agent that sends null to empty the list gets a 200 and no change at all. To clear it, send [].\",\n        \"title\": \"Suggested Replies Reply Card\"\n      },\n      \"suggested_replies_task_message\": {\n        \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n            \"items\": {\n              \"type\": \"string\"\n            },\n            \"type\": \"array\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"description\": \"Replace the 建議回覆 list offered under a 任務 message box (T-122) wholesale. Same bounds as suggested_replies_reply_card — at most 20 entries, each trimmed and at most 120 runes, over either is a 422 that writes nothing, and an explicit empty array is legal — but a SEPARATE list by owner ruling: answering a 請示卡 and writing to a task in progress are different conversations, and patching one list never touches the other. Read the current list from get_settings before sending: this replaces it, it does not append. 🔴 null is NOT \\\"clear\\\": an omitted field and an explicit null both mean LEAVE THIS LIST UNCHANGED, so an agent that sends null to empty the list gets a 200 and no change at all. To clear it, send [].\",\n        \"title\": \"Suggested Replies Task Message\"\n      },\n      \"agent_token_ttl\": {\n        \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"integer\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"title\": \"Agent Token Ttl\"\n      },\n      \"owner_token_ttl\": {\n        \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"integer\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"title\": \"Owner Token Ttl\"\n      },\n      \"updater_auto_update\": {\n        \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"title\": \"Updater Auto Update\"\n      },\n      \"updater_receive_beta\": {\n        \"anyOf\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"type\": \"null\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"title\": \"Updater Receive Beta\"\n      }\n    },\n    \"additionalProperties\": false,\n    \"type\": \"object\"\n  },\n  \"name\": \"update_settings\"\n}"}}
func HandleUpdateSettingsApiSettingsPatch(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
}

//oc:doc "Read the 系統互動 block of the boot context — the studio handbook every agent and outsource worker reads first (T-791e).\n\nIt is an OVERLAY over the shipped seed (`seeds/system_interaction.md`): ``is_default=true`` means nobody has edited it and you are reading the factory text, ``false`` means you are reading an edit. ``has_seed`` reports that a factory version exists to reset back to.\n\nBefore T-791e this block had no editable representation at all — changing one sentence cost a release."
//oc:route GET /api/system-interaction
//oc:id handle_get_system_interaction_api_system_interaction_get
//oc:summary "Read the 系統互動 block of the boot context — the shared studio handbook every agent reads at boot. Folded: the owner's edit when one exists, otherwise the shipped factory seed, with is_default saying which of the two you are holding and has_seed saying a factory version exists to go back to. The reply carries size_chars/cap_chars (this document's own size limit, in characters) and is_default/has_seed, so a caller can size an edit before making it and can tell an edited block from the shipped one."
//oc:resp 200 application/json ref=BootDocumentDTO "Successful Response"
//oc:errors std
//oc:mcp {"include":true,"order":107,"name":"get_system_interaction","description":"Read the 系統互動 block of the boot context — the shared studio handbook every agent reads at boot. Folded: the owner's edit when one exists, otherwise the shipped factory seed, with is_default saying which of the two you are holding and has_seed saying a factory version exists to go back to. The reply carries size_chars/cap_chars (this document's own size limit, in characters) and is_default/has_seed, so a caller can size an edit before making it and can tell an edited block from the shipped one.","legacy":{"descriptor":"{\n      \"description\": \"Read the 系統互動 block of the boot context — the shared studio handbook every agent reads at boot. Folded: the owner's edit when one exists, otherwise the shipped factory seed, with is_default saying which of the two you are holding and has_seed saying a factory version exists to go back to. The reply carries size_chars/cap_chars (this document's own size limit, in characters) and is_default/has_seed, so a caller can size an edit before making it and can tell an edited block from the shipped one.\",\n      \"inputSchema\": {\n        \"properties\": {},\n        \"type\": \"object\"\n      },\n      \"name\": \"get_system_interaction\"\n    }"}}
func HandleGetSystemInteractionApiSystemInteractionGet(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
}

//oc:doc "Replace the EDITABLE HALF of the 系統互動 block: ``{body}`` (T-791e; body-only since T-3201).\n\nWrites an OVERLAY — the shipped seed is never modified, so ``/api/system-interaction/reset`` can always reach the factory text. ``body`` is REQUIRED (a replace must never infer \"empty\" from a missing key); ``allow_shrink`` (default false) must be set explicitly to replace an existing body with an empty one. The read-only head is not part of the request and cannot be: the server joins the shipped one back on, so no caller has any way to write it. The ``doc.cap_chars.system_interaction`` cap is checked UNCONDITIONALLY against the STORED result — ``allow_shrink`` governs the opposite direction and is not a bypass.\n\nA save whose folded result is IDENTICAL to what is stored writes nothing and retains NO version: these blocks are edited from a text box, and idle saves would otherwise push the version worth going back to off the end of the retained list.\n\nGovernance write (owner or the admin 助理): this text lands in every agent's boot context."
//oc:route POST /api/system-interaction
//oc:id handle_replace_system_interaction_api_system_interaction_post
//oc:summary "Replace the EDITABLE HALF of the 系統互動 block of the boot context ({body}) — the handbook every agent reads at boot. body is REQUIRED and unknown keys are rejected; emptying a body that had content needs allow_shrink=true. This document carries NO read-only head today (T-6f44, owner's decision 4 removed it), so the body IS the whole document; the head machinery still exists for the kinds that do carry one, and there is no way to write a head on any face. The stored result is judged against the doc.cap_chars.system_interaction cap unconditionally, and the refusal tells you what you wrote, the cap, and what is already stored. The shipped seed is never overwritten, so reset_system_interaction always gets the factory text back; the version this write replaces is retained in the document history (a save that changes nothing retains nothing). Owner or admin assistant only. Answers with a bounded receipt (``kind``, ``key``, ``is_default``, ``size_chars``, ``cap_chars``, ``sha256``), not the document — call ``get_system_interaction`` when you need the rest."
//oc:body application/json req ref=BootDocumentReplaceDTO
//oc:resp 200 application/json ref=BootDocumentReceiptDTO "Successful Response"
//oc:errors std
//oc:mcp {"include":true,"order":108,"name":"replace_system_interaction","description":"Replace the EDITABLE HALF of the 系統互動 block of the boot context ({body}) — the handbook every agent reads at boot. body is REQUIRED and unknown keys are rejected; emptying a body that had content needs allow_shrink=true. This document carries NO read-only head today (T-6f44, owner's decision 4 removed it), so the body IS the whole document; the head machinery still exists for the kinds that do carry one, and there is no way to write a head on any face. The stored result is judged against the doc.cap_chars.system_interaction cap unconditionally, and the refusal tells you what you wrote, the cap, and what is already stored. The shipped seed is never overwritten, so reset_system_interaction always gets the factory text back; the version this write replaces is retained in the document history (a save that changes nothing retains nothing). Owner or admin assistant only. Answers with a bounded receipt (``kind``, ``key``, ``is_default``, ``size_chars``, ``cap_chars``, ``sha256``), not the document — call ``get_system_interaction`` when you need the rest.","legacy":{"descriptor":"{\n      \"description\": \"Replace the EDITABLE HALF of the 系統互動 block of the boot context ({body}) — the handbook every agent reads at boot. body is REQUIRED and unknown keys are rejected; emptying a body that had content needs allow_shrink=true. This document carries NO read-only head today (T-6f44, owner's decision 4 removed it), so the body IS the whole document; the head machinery still exists for the kinds that do carry one, and there is no way to write a head on any face. The stored result is judged against the doc.cap_chars.system_interaction cap unconditionally, and the refusal tells you what you wrote, the cap, and what is already stored. The shipped seed is never overwritten, so reset_system_interaction always gets the factory text back; the version this write replaces is retained in the document history (a save that changes nothing retains nothing). Owner or admin assistant only. Answers with a bounded receipt (``kind``, ``key``, ``is_default``, ``size_chars``, ``cap_chars``, ``sha256``), not the document — call ``get_system_interaction`` when you need the rest.\",\n      \"inputSchema\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"allow_shrink\": {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n          },\n          \"body\": {\n            \"description\": \"The ENTIRE editable half of the system-interaction document, not an addition to it - and this is the one every agent reads while booting. Sending a fragment answers 200 and permanently drops the rest of the body, so read the current body with get_system_interaction first and fold your change into it. The read-only head is not part of this and cannot be sent. The guards catch only the extremes: emptying a body that had content needs allow_shrink, and the character cap is enforced. A write that keeps a few paragraphs and loses the rest is neither, and passes without comment - while every agent that boots afterwards reads the shortened version as though it were the whole rulebook.\",\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"body\"\n        ],\n        \"type\": \"object\"\n      },\n      \"name\": \"replace_system_interaction\"\n    }"}}
func HandleReplaceSystemInteractionApiSystemInteractionPost(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
}

//oc:doc "Reset the 系統互動 block to the SHIPPED seed (T-791e): an idempotent tombstone of the overlay, so the folded read falls back to `seeds/system_interaction.md` (``is_default`` → true).\n\nNO length cap is checked on this path, matching ``reset_role``/``reset_insight``: the factory text is part of the product, so a cap the owner raised or set afterwards must never be able to block the way back to it. This is the route that has to work when a bad edit has stopped agents from booting, and at that moment there may be nobody online to ask — it needs no agent, no MCP client and no member identity, only the owner's token.\n\nThe discarded overlay is retained as a document-history revision, so the reset is itself recoverable. Resetting an already-default block writes nothing and retains nothing."
