//oc:doc "Partial manual edit — only supplied fields change. Agent floor: content fields (purpose / fields / sop_md / learnings) are agent-editable; ``assignee`` is GOVERNANCE — a caller below admin_agent supplying it is a 403 (T-6020). ``assignee`` is {\"kind\":\"staff\",\"member_id\":…} or {\"kind\":\"outsource\",\"model\":…,\"effort\":…,\"copies\":N}; {} unsets it. Unknown keys are REJECTED (422) rather than silently dropped: this endpoint writes the same learnings document as ``write_task_learnings``, which spells the field ``text`` instead of ``learnings`` — sending the wrong name used to answer 200 having written nothing (T-2d99). Omitting a field remains legal; only unrecognised names are refused. The SOP and the learnings are judged by two SEPARATE caps, reported as ``sop_md_cap_chars`` and ``learnings_cap_chars``; the older ``cap_chars`` is DEPRECATED — it carries the LEARNINGS cap only and says nothing about sop_md, so read ``sop_md_cap_chars`` for the SOP."
//oc:route POST /api/task-manuals/{type_key}
//oc:id handle_update_task_manual_api_task_manuals__type_key__post
//oc:summary "Edit a task manual (partial; content fields agent-editable; assignee = owner/admin agent). An outsource assignee may select runtime claude/codex; absent = claude. Only the fields you name change, so omitting a field is safe — but unknown keys are rejected rather than dropped: the learnings doc goes in learnings (NOT text — that is write_task_learnings' field name). The SOP and the learnings are judged by two SEPARATE caps: read sop_md_cap_chars and learnings_cap_chars. The older cap_chars is DEPRECATED — it carries the LEARNINGS cap only and says nothing about sop_md, so read sop_md_cap_chars for the SOP. Answers with a bounded receipt (``type_key``, ``updated_ts``, ``learnings_chars``, ``learnings_cap_chars``, ``learnings_sha256``, ``sop_md_chars``, ``sop_md_cap_chars``, ``sop_md_sha256``), not the manual — call ``get_task_manual`` when you need the rest."
//oc:param path type_key req
//oc:body application/json req ref=TaskManualUpdateDTO
//oc:resp 200 application/json ref=TaskManualReceiptDTO "Successful Response"
//oc:errors std
//oc:mcp {"include":true,"order":97,"name":"update_task_manual","description":"Edit a task manual (partial; content fields agent-editable; assignee = owner/admin agent). An outsource assignee may select runtime claude/codex; absent = claude. Only the fields you name change, so omitting a field is safe — but unknown keys are rejected rather than dropped: the learnings doc goes in learnings (NOT text — that is write_task_learnings' field name). The SOP and the learnings are judged by two SEPARATE caps: read sop_md_cap_chars and learnings_cap_chars. The older cap_chars is DEPRECATED — it carries the LEARNINGS cap only and says nothing about sop_md, so read sop_md_cap_chars for the SOP. Answers with a bounded receipt (``type_key``, ``updated_ts``, ``learnings_chars``, ``learnings_cap_chars``, ``learnings_sha256``, ``sop_md_chars``, ``sop_md_cap_chars``, ``sop_md_sha256``), not the manual — call ``get_task_manual`` when you need the rest.","legacy":{"descriptor":"{\n      \"description\": \"Edit a task manual (partial; content fields agent-editable; assignee = owner/admin agent). An outsource assignee may select runtime claude/codex; absent = claude. Only the fields you name change, so omitting a field is safe — but unknown keys are rejected rather than dropped: the learnings doc goes in learnings (NOT text — that is write_task_learnings' field name). The SOP and the learnings are judged by two SEPARATE caps: read sop_md_cap_chars and learnings_cap_chars. The older cap_chars is DEPRECATED — it carries the LEARNINGS cap only and says nothing about sop_md, so read sop_md_cap_chars for the SOP. Answers with a bounded receipt (``type_key``, ``updated_ts``, ``learnings_chars``, ``learnings_cap_chars``, ``learnings_sha256``, ``sop_md_chars``, ``sop_md_cap_chars``, ``sop_md_sha256``), not the manual — call ``get_task_manual`` when you need the rest.\",\n      \"inputSchema\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"assignee\": {\n            \"anyOf\": [\n              {\n                \"additionalProperties\": true,\n                \"type\": \"object\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"type\": \"null\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"default\": null,\n            \"description\": \"Replacement assignee object for the type - governance, so a caller below admin-agent supplying it is a 403. It is a WHOLE-OBJECT replacement, not a merge: what you send becomes the entire assignee, so an outsource assignee re-sent as kind plus machine silently drops the copies and effort that were there before, and an empty object clears the assignee altogether. Both answer 200. The same checks as the create face apply - kind must be 'staff' or 'outsource', an outsource runtime, effort and copies are range-checked and machine must resolve - and so does the same gap: unknown sub-keys are stored verbatim and never read, and member_id is only tested for being non-empty, never looked up.\",\n            \"title\": \"Assignee\"\n          },\n          \"display_name\": {\n            \"anyOf\": [\n              {\n                \"type\": \"string\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"type\": \"null\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"default\": null,\n            \"description\": \"The manual's human-facing name — what list_task_manuals shows and what people match on when they pick a type — as opposed to type_key, the immutable id you address it by. Pass it to rename a type without breaking anything that references the key (leading/trailing whitespace is trimmed). Omitted leaves the stored name untouched, like every other field on this partial update.\",\n            \"title\": \"Display Name\"\n          },\n          \"fields\": {\n            \"anyOf\": [\n              {\n                \"items\": {\n                  \"properties\": {\n                    \"is_key\": {\n                      \"default\": false,\n                      \"title\": \"Is Key\",\n                      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n                    },\n                    \"name\": {\n                      \"title\": \"Name\",\n                      \"type\": \"string\"\n                    },\n                    \"required\": {\n                      \"default\": false,\n                      \"title\": \"Required\",\n                      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n                    }\n                  },\n                  \"required\": [\n                    \"name\"\n                  ],\n                  \"type\": \"object\",\n                  \"additionalProperties\": false\n                },\n                \"type\": \"array\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"type\": \"null\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"default\": null,\n            \"title\": \"Fields\"\n          },\n          \"learnings\": {\n            \"anyOf\": [\n              {\n                \"type\": \"string\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"type\": \"null\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"default\": null,\n            \"title\": \"Learnings\",\n            \"description\": \"Replaces the WHOLE learnings doc of this manual - and unlike write_task_learnings, which writes the same document, this path has NO wipe guard. write_task_learnings refuses to empty a doc that had content unless allow_shrink is set; here {\\\"learnings\\\": \\\"\\\"} is simply accepted and answers 200 with the document gone. Only the character cap is checked. Because both calls write the same doc, the safety you get depends purely on which one you happened to use, and nothing in either response says which protections applied. Omit the field to leave the doc alone; send the full current text with your change folded in when you do mean to write. Also note the field names are NOT interchangeable between the two calls: this one is 'learnings', write_task_learnings takes 'text'.\"\n          },\n          \"purpose\": {\n            \"anyOf\": [\n              {\n                \"type\": \"string\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"type\": \"null\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"default\": null,\n            \"description\": \"Replaces the manual's whole purpose text. Nothing validates it - no cap, no wipe guard, no format check - so an empty string clears it and a fragment replaces the rest, both answering 200. Omit the field to leave it alone; send the full text when you do mean to write.\",\n            \"title\": \"Purpose\"\n          },\n          \"sop_md\": {\n            \"anyOf\": [\n              {\n                \"type\": \"string\"\n              },\n              {\n                \"type\": \"null\"\n              }\n            ],\n            \"default\": null,\n            \"description\": \"Replaces the WHOLE SOP of this manual, and it is the only way in - there is no patch-by-anchor counterpart for this document the way patch_task_learnings exists for the learnings half. The only guard is the character cap: unlike write_task_learnings, there is NO wipe guard here, so an empty string is accepted and clears the SOP, and a fragment silently replaces everything else. Both answer 200. Read the current SOP first and fold your change into it. Omit the field to leave it alone.\",\n            \"title\": \"Sop Md\"\n          },\n          \"type_key\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"type_key\"\n        ],\n        \"additionalProperties\": false,\n        \"type\": \"object\"\n      },\n      \"name\": \"update_task_manual\"\n    }"}}
func HandleUpdateTaskManualApiTaskManualsTypeKeyPost(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request, typeKey string) {
}

//oc:doc "Whole-doc replace of a type's learnings (MCP ``write_task_learnings`` — the agent's task-close write-back; the replace_lessons shape). Unknown type → 404."
//oc:route POST /api/task-manuals/{type_key}/learnings
//oc:id handle_write_task_learnings_api_task_manuals__type_key__learnings_post
//oc:summary "Whole-doc replace of a type's learnings (task-close write-back). The doc text goes in text (NOT learnings — that is update_task_manual's field name); text is REQUIRED and unknown keys are rejected. Wiping existing learnings needs allow_shrink=true. Answers with a bounded receipt (``type_key``, ``size_chars``, ``cap_chars``, ``sha256``), not the learnings text — call ``get_task_manual`` when you need the rest."
//oc:param path type_key req
//oc:body application/json req ref=TaskLearningsReplaceDTO
//oc:resp 200 application/json ref=TaskLearningsWriteReceiptDTO "Successful Response"
//oc:errors std
//oc:mcp {"include":true,"order":99,"name":"write_task_learnings","description":"Whole-doc replace of a type's learnings (task-close write-back). The doc text goes in text (NOT learnings — that is update_task_manual's field name); text is REQUIRED and unknown keys are rejected. Wiping existing learnings needs allow_shrink=true. Answers with a bounded receipt (``type_key``, ``size_chars``, ``cap_chars``, ``sha256``), not the learnings text — call ``get_task_manual`` when you need the rest.","legacy":{"descriptor":"{\n      \"description\": \"Whole-doc replace of a type's learnings (task-close write-back). The doc text goes in text (NOT learnings — that is update_task_manual's field name); text is REQUIRED and unknown keys are rejected. Wiping existing learnings needs allow_shrink=true. Answers with a bounded receipt (``type_key``, ``size_chars``, ``cap_chars``, ``sha256``), not the learnings text — call ``get_task_manual`` when you need the rest.\",\n      \"inputSchema\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"allow_shrink\": {\n            \"default\": false,\n            \"title\": \"Allow Shrink\",\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n          },\n          \"text\": {\n            \"default\": \"\",\n            \"title\": \"Text\",\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"The ENTIRE learnings doc, not an addition to it: whatever you send becomes the whole document and everything else is gone. The field name says 'text' but the seam is a whole-doc replace, so sending the paragraph you wanted to add answers 200 and permanently drops the rest. Read the current doc first and send it back with your change folded in, or use patch_task_learnings, which edits by anchor instead. TWO guards stand here and they behave differently. The wipe guard catches only the extreme case - emptying a doc that had content - and allow_shrink=true switches it off; either way, a replace that merely loses most of the text passes without comment. The second is the learnings size cap, and it is UNCONDITIONAL: allow_shrink is not a bypass for it, it refuses any text over the cap that is not shorter than what is stored, and its refusal names your length, the cap and the current length. Note the sibling update_task_manual writes this same document through its 'learnings' field: it enforces the same cap, but it has NO wipe guard, so an empty string sent there erases the doc without asking.\"\n          },\n          \"type_key\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"type_key\",\n          \"text\"\n        ],\n        \"additionalProperties\": false,\n        \"type\": \"object\"\n      },\n      \"name\": \"write_task_learnings\"\n    }"}}
func HandleWriteTaskLearningsApiTaskManualsTypeKeyLearningsPost(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request, typeKey string) {
}

//oc:doc "Anchor-addressed PATCH of a type's learnings (MCP ``patch_task_learnings`` — the learnings twin of ``patch_lessons``). The write cost scales with the CHANGE, not the doc: a whole-doc ``write_task_learnings`` stops fitting in one model output as the learnings grow (30k chars observed, and re-typing the whole doc silently risks transcription loss), so this is the primary write seam and whole-doc replace stays the last resort.\n\nSemantics: ``edits`` apply IN ORDER against the manual's current learnings; each non-empty ``old`` must match the current text exactly once (0 hits or >1 hits → flat 400, WHOLE batch rejected, zero writes); an empty ``old`` appends ``new`` at the end. Concurrency is last-write-wins with the unique anchor as a natural optimistic lock: a concurrent write that moved the anchor turns the next patch into a 400, never a silent mis-splice. A patch that empties the doc (or shrinks it below a tenth of its size) is refused unless ``allow_shrink=true`` — the r-76 wipe-guard posture. Unknown type → 404.\n\nWrite authz is the agent floor — identical to ``write_task_learnings`` (manual CONTENT is agent-editable). The receipt carries ``size``/``sha256`` verification anchors over the resulting learnings."
//oc:route POST /api/task-manuals/{type_key}/learnings/patch
//oc:id handle_patch_task_learnings_api_task_manuals__type_key__learnings_patch_post
//oc:summary "Patch a type's learnings by unique anchors ({edits:[{old,new}]}) — the learnings twin of patch_lessons, so the write cost scales with the CHANGE, not the whole (30k-char) doc, and re-typing the whole doc can no longer silently drop content. Edits apply in order; a non-empty old must match the current learnings EXACTLY ONCE (0 or >1 hits reject the WHOLE batch with a 400, zero writes — the unique anchor also acts as an optimistic lock); an empty old appends. Wiping the doc, or shrinking it below a tenth, needs allow_shrink=true."
//oc:param path type_key req
//oc:body application/json req ref=TaskLearningsPatchDTO
//oc:resp 200 application/json ref=TaskLearningsPatchResultDTO "Successful Response"
//oc:errors std
//oc:mcp {"include":true,"order":100,"name":"patch_task_learnings","description":"Patch a type's learnings by unique anchors ({edits:[{old,new}]}) — the learnings twin of patch_lessons, so the write cost scales with the CHANGE, not the whole (30k-char) doc, and re-typing the whole doc can no longer silently drop content. Edits apply in order; a non-empty old must match the current learnings EXACTLY ONCE (0 or >1 hits reject the WHOLE batch with a 400, zero writes — the unique anchor also acts as an optimistic lock); an empty old appends. Wiping the doc, or shrinking it below a tenth, needs allow_shrink=true.","legacy":{"descriptor":"{\n      \"description\": \"Patch a type's learnings by unique anchors ({edits:[{old,new}]}) — the learnings twin of patch_lessons, so the write cost scales with the CHANGE, not the whole (30k-char) doc, and re-typing the whole doc can no longer silently drop content. Edits apply in order; a non-empty old must match the current learnings EXACTLY ONCE (0 or >1 hits reject the WHOLE batch with a 400, zero writes — the unique anchor also acts as an optimistic lock); an empty old appends. Wiping the doc, or shrinking it below a tenth, needs allow_shrink=true.\",\n      \"inputSchema\": {\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"allow_shrink\": {\n            \"default\": false,\n            \"title\": \"Allow Shrink\",\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n          },\n          \"edits\": {\n            \"items\": {\n              \"properties\": {\n                \"new\": {\n                  \"default\": \"\",\n                  \"title\": \"New\",\n                  \"type\": \"string\"\n                },\n                \"old\": {\n                  \"default\": \"\",\n                  \"title\": \"Old\",\n                  \"type\": \"string\"\n                }\n              },\n              \"title\": \"LessonsEditDTO\",\n              \"type\": \"object\",\n              \"additionalProperties\": false\n            },\n            \"title\": \"Edits\",\n            \"type\": \"array\"\n          },\n          \"type_key\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"required\": [\n          \"type_key\",\n          \"edits\"\n        ],\n        \"additionalProperties\": false,\n        \"type\": \"object\"\n      },\n      \"name\": \"patch_task_learnings\"\n    }"}}
